## 🚀 How to Run Locally

### Prerequisites
- Java 21 installed
- Apache Tomcat 10.1 installed
- MySQL 8.0 installed
- Eclipse IDE with Maven support
- Git installed

### Steps

**1. Clone the repository**
```bash
git clone https://github.com/Madhavi-Gurram/FashionStore-Java-Fullstack.git
```

**2. Import into Eclipse**

File → Import → Maven → Existing Maven Projects
Browse to cloned folder → Finish


**3. Create Database**

Open MySQL Workbench and run:
```sql
CREATE DATABASE fashion_store;
USE fashion_store;
```
Then run the complete schema SQL provided in the project.

**4. Configure DB Connection**

Open `src/main/java/com/fashionstore/util/DBConnection.java`:
```java
private static final String URL =
    "jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/fashion_store";
private static final String USER = "root";
private static final String PASSWORD = "your_mysql_password";
```

**5. Maven Update**

Right click project → Maven → Update Project (Alt+F5) → OK


**6. Run on Tomcat**

Right click project → Run As → Run on Server
Select Apache Tomcat 10.1 → Finish


**7. Open in Browser**

http://localhost:8080/FashionStore/home


**8. Setup Admin Account**
```sql
UPDATE users
SET is_admin = TRUE
WHERE email = 'your_registered_email@gmail.com';
```

Then visit Admin Panel:

http://localhost:8080/FashionStore/admin


---

## 🌊 Application Flow

User Visits Home
↓
Browse Products by Category / Search / Filter
↓
View Product Detail → Select Size → Add to Cart
↓
View Cart → Proceed to Checkout
↓
Enter Delivery Details → Select Payment
↓
Place Order → Order Confirmation
↓
Track Order → View Progress Bar
↓
View Order History → My Orders Page


---

## 🔐 Security Features

✅ BCrypt Password Hashing
→ Passwords never stored as plain text

✅ Session Management
→ User sessions handled securely

✅ Admin Role Check
→ Admin pages protected from regular users

✅ JSP inside WEB-INF
→ JSP files not directly accessible via URL

✅ Server-side Validation
→ All forms validated on server

✅ Client-side Validation
→ JavaScript validation before form submit


